1
00:00:00,180 --> 00:00:05,637
We are team bob the builder, presenting synthetic card dispute
resolution for Track Three.

2
00:00:05,757 --> 00:00:10,665
The workbench helps analysts investigate disputes and record
auditable outcomes.

3
00:00:10,785 --> 00:00:13,549
All records and financial effects are fictional.

4
00:00:14,947 --> 00:00:17,019
Zetaris retrieves source facts.

5
00:00:17,139 --> 00:00:20,328
The Investigator proposes an outcome through Nightshift.

6
00:00:20,448 --> 00:00:24,507
A code based critic checks policy, amounts and citations.

7
00:00:24,627 --> 00:00:27,268
A separate Reviewer challenges the evidence.

8
00:00:27,388 --> 00:00:33,450
Both checks must accept the same proposal before the database
writer rechecks current facts and commits.

9
00:00:34,747 --> 00:00:40,291
Case D P twenty has a captured transaction of one hundred and
fourteen Singapore dollars.

10
00:00:40,411 --> 00:00:45,224
A merchant promise is present, but the required refund
confirmation is missing.

11
00:00:45,344 --> 00:00:51,319
In this recorded live run, the Investigator requested evidence
and the critic and Reviewer accepted.

12
00:00:51,439 --> 00:00:56,056
Two Nightshift calls produced a saved evidence request with no
credit effect.

13
00:00:56,176 --> 00:00:59,817
Recovery reused the same decision with zero model calls.

14
00:00:59,937 --> 00:01:02,064
Memory was disabled for this run.

15
00:01:08,113 --> 00:01:11,058
Case D P fourteen makes the arithmetic clear.

16
00:01:11,178 --> 00:01:16,344
One hundred Singapore dollars was captured, and the merchant
already refunded forty.

17
00:01:16,464 --> 00:01:21,407
The remaining amount is sixty dollars, recorded as a separate
simulated credit.

18
00:01:21,527 --> 00:01:25,691
This rehearsal uses scripted models and a real isolated
database.

19
00:01:25,811 --> 00:01:29,196
An identical request reuses the original decision.

20
00:01:29,316 --> 00:01:35,510
A fresh attempt is rejected, so processing the case again cannot
create a second effective credit.

21
00:01:37,680 --> 00:01:42,009
For D P three, the allowed credit is two hundred Singapore
dollars.

22
00:01:42,129 --> 00:01:46,062
The test deliberately proposes two hundred dollars and one cent.

23
00:01:46,182 --> 00:01:49,674
The critic rejects the extra cent and allows one correction.

24
00:01:49,794 --> 00:01:53,762
The corrected proposal passes the critic and Reviewer before the
write.

25
00:01:53,882 --> 00:01:58,568
This is an injected test fault, not a spontaneous live model
mistake.

26
00:02:01,947 --> 00:02:08,943
A later investigation, D P seventeen, recalls the earlier D P
fourteen decision through H mem.

27
00:02:09,063 --> 00:02:14,226
The workflow verifies the committed receipt and customer
ownership against source records.

28
00:02:14,346 --> 00:02:18,911
Memory supplies context, while policy determines eligibility.

29
00:02:19,031 --> 00:02:23,892
This rehearsal uses the real reference engine with mock
embeddings and scripted models.

30
00:02:24,012 --> 00:02:27,722
Retrying memory storage never repeats the financial action.

31
00:02:28,147 --> 00:02:40,775
The new Unified Semantic Layer joins three independent
connectors: PostgreSQL with forty cases, a CSV file with four
merchant records, and a REST source with three history records.

32
00:02:40,895 --> 00:02:46,049
For D P twenty, the join returns two merchant records and two
history records.

33
00:02:46,169 --> 00:02:49,625
This optional preview cannot authorize financial actions.

34
00:02:49,745 --> 00:02:54,030
Source freshness and a shared cross-source snapshot remain
unverified.

35
00:02:57,413 --> 00:03:00,463
This separate quality test contains two records.

36
00:03:00,583 --> 00:03:02,777
One references an existing case.

37
00:03:02,897 --> 00:03:05,541
The orphan references a nonexistent case.

38
00:03:05,661 --> 00:03:08,848
Zetaris detects exactly one invalid record.

39
00:03:08,968 --> 00:03:13,202
The result proves that the foreign key check catches broken
relationships.

40
00:03:13,322 --> 00:03:16,418
It does not prove document truth or source freshness.

41
00:03:17,313 --> 00:03:25,449
The latest recorded suite passed three hundred and twenty eight
application tests and sixteen reference checks, with no failures
or skips.

42
00:03:25,569 --> 00:03:28,304
Rehearsals cover all four outcomes shown here.

43
00:03:28,424 --> 00:03:35,174
Real models still vary: the Reviewer appeared overly
conservative on D P twenty nine and stopped without writing.

44
00:03:36,980 --> 00:03:45,383
The contribution combines observable agent collaboration,
duplicate prevention, verified memory and inspectable source
quality.

45
00:03:45,503 --> 00:03:49,768
Next steps are broader document support and source freshness
metadata.
